Modifications made to the original files
----------------------------------------
As required by section 4(b) of the License, the following changes have been made
to the files as distributed by Adobe:

1. Stylesheets were renamed from `.css` to `.scss` and the corresponding imports
   in the component files were updated. The CSS content itself was unchanged.

2. The per-stylesheet `@import "./theme"` and `@import "./utilities"` rules were
   removed. Both files are now loaded once from the application's root layout
   instead, so their contents are no longer duplicated into every CSS chunk.
   Where a stylesheet depended on another component's stylesheet (`./Form`,
   `./TextField`), the `@import` was changed to `@use`, since Sass `@import` is
   deprecated. No style declarations were added, removed or altered.

3. Small changes to keep the repository's lint, type and formatting checks
   passing, none of which alter component behaviour:
   - Story files import story types from the framework package
     (`@storybook/nextjs-vite`) rather than the renderer package
     (`@storybook/react`).
   - `GridList.stories.tsx`: `alt=""` added to the demo images, which are
     decorative because each is labelled by the adjacent `<Text>` and by the
     item's `textValue`.
   - `Meter.tsx`, `ProgressBar.tsx`: the `as any` on inline styles carrying a CSS
     custom property narrowed to `as CSSProperties`.
   - `ColorWheel.tsx`: an empty `interface … extends Omit<…> {}` rewritten as an
     equivalent type alias.
   - Two unused declarations removed, `let` narrowed to `const` where never
     reassigned, and the files formatted with the project's Prettier config.
   - `CommandPalette.tsx`, `Dialog.stories.tsx`, `Modal.stories.tsx`: the three
     `autoFocus` props annotated with a justified `jsx-a11y/no-autofocus`
     suppression. The props themselves were not changed.
   - `Toast.stories.tsx`: the hardcoded `title: "Toast"` removed so Storybook's
     automatic titling groups it under `react-aria/` with the other stories in
     this directory, rather than alongside the application's own.

4. `Button.tsx`: the hardcoded `className` is now composed with the caller's
   `className` instead of replacing it. As distributed, any class name passed to
   a Button was silently dropped. The classes the kit applies are unchanged.

5. Accessibility test settings, after the project's Storybook a11y checks were
   made blocking by default. No component behaviour was changed:
   - `Tooltip.stories.tsx`: `aria-label="Save"` added to the icon-only demo
     button, which had no accessible name. A tooltip labels on hover and focus
     but does not name the element.
   - `Meter.stories.tsx`: the `aria-allowed-attr` axe rule disabled for this
     story, with the reason recorded inline. It is a known axe false positive
     against react-aria's `role="meter progressbar"`.
   - `Calendar.stories.tsx`, `RangeCalendar.stories.tsx`: the
     `landmark-banner-is-top-level` axe rule disabled for these stories. Both
     render a bare `<header>`, which is a `banner` landmark only when rendered
     outside a sectioning element — an artifact of the story canvas, not of the
     component in a page.

6. Every hardcoded `system-ui` font family in the stylesheets was replaced
   with `var(--font-family, system-ui)`, so an application can set a brand
   font in one declaration rather than in 34 files. The boilerplate leaves
   the custom property undeclared, so the rendered font is unchanged.

7. innn.it brand styling appended to the end of five stylesheets, after each
   file's own rules, so the additions read as a distinct block rather than
   interleaving with the vendor's declarations:
   - `Button.scss`: flat pill-button variant (`.pill-button`,
     `.pill-button[data-variant="secondary"]`, `.pill-button.cta-button`).
   - `TextField.scss`: taller input/textarea sizing, a filled read-only
     state, and full-ink description text.
   - `Dialog.scss`: a larger, bolder dialog title.
   - `Switch.scss`: an outlined track/handle in place of the kit's filled
     switch.
   - `Modal.scss`: a wider max-width for the dialog frame.
   No existing declaration was edited or removed; each addition is a
   separate, source-order-later rule.
